# What the package must not carry. The extension needs only dist/src, media
# and the manifest; everything else here is notes, corpus or tooling.
# `vsce ls --tree` is the check: it must list nothing outside those three.
#
# Excludes only, no `!` negations. An allowlist was tried first (`*` then
# `!dist/src/**`): vsce re-included every sourcemap that `*.map` excluded, so
# the negations were winning regardless of order. A bare `*.map` also does not
# reach into subdirectories here, which is why `dist/**/*.map` is named too.
HANDOFF.md
ROADMAP.md
bench/**
userdocs/**
examples/**
lisp_test_files/**
src/**
test/**
dist/test/**
node_modules/**
.npm-cache/**
.dsh-code-index/**
.vscode/**
.git/**
dist/**/*.map
*.map
*.ts
*.vsix
*.code-workspace
tsconfig.json
package-lock.json
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.npmrc
.vscodeignore
